# Redirect rules for the Cloudflare asset server. Copied into dist/ by
# scripts/build-dist.mjs, which the asset server reads from the deployment root and does
# not serve.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. Limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF RULES (24 Aug 2026).
#
# It used to carry eleven 301s covering the .html forms and two renamed paths. Those
# existed for one reason: those URLs had been indexed for months on
# indianinprague.jains.es, and the asset server's own built-in redirect is a 307
# TEMPORARY, which tells Google the OLD URL is still canonical — the opposite of the
# truth after a permanent move.
#
# guldaarbazaar.com is a new hostname with no indexing history and no inbound links, so
# there is nothing for a 301 to consolidate. The built-in 307 on /wardrobe.html is
# therefore harmless here: it still resolves for anyone who types the .html form, it just
# carries no ranking signal that could be misattributed.
#
# If a path on THIS domain ever gets indexed and then moves, add its 301 here. The
# reasoning above is the test for whether a rule belongs in this file.

# 26 Sep 2026: /partner split into one page per audience. /partner was indexed and linked
# (and sent round on WhatsApp), so it gets a real 301. The fragment survives the redirect,
# and partner.js forwards #retailer to /partner/retailer.
/partner /partner/merchant 301
